    "type": "question",
    "label": "75",
    "prompt": "Super chain rule! Let $y=f(g(h(x)))$. Find $y'$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y'=f'(g(h(x)))g'(h(x))h'(x)$.\n\nApply the chain rule to each of the three layers.",
      "worked": "Let $u=g(h(x))$ and $v=h(x)$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=f'(u)\\frac{du}{dx}\\\\y'&=f'(g(v))g'(v)\\frac{dv}{dx}\\\\y'&=f'(g(h(x)))g'(h(x))h'(x).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
